Description: Linux-native WebAuthn/FIDO2 authenticator bridge
 Linux WebAuthn provides a native Linux WebAuthn/FIDO2 authenticator bridge
 for desktop systems. It integrates fingerprint verification, TPM-backed
 credential handling, D-Bus, and a virtual FIDO HID authenticator so that
 browsers can use local Linux authentication hardware for WebAuthn.
 .
 The service runs in the logged-in user's systemd user session and does not
 require the authenticator daemon itself to run as root.
